--- 1B: Orthogonality check: mean stringency vs mean fiscal deployment ---
  r(mean S, mean F_CP)    = +0.149
  r(mean S, mean F_DI)    = -0.040
  r(mean S, mean F_total) = +0.096
  r(mean S, CP share)     = +0.078

  INTERPRETATION: Near-zero correlations confirm that fiscal composition
  was driven by institutional capacity, political preferences, and pre-
  existing safety nets rather than by contemporaneous pandemic severity.
  This near-orthogonality is the key identifying condition: the S*F_CP
  interaction provides within-country variation that is not confounded by
  common time shocks (absorbed by quarter FE) or country heterogeneity
  (absorbed by country FE). Paper reference: Section 4.2, empirical_draft.

