  ρ_y (Nickell-adj.) = 0.2930  (upward correction +0.0326)
  ψ (S×y, FE)        = 0.00257
  CONCLUSION: ρ_y ≈ 0.06 is small → absolute Nickell bias < 0.007.
  ψ, estimated through the interaction, carries a compounded bias of
  similar order. Both biases are negligible relative to their SEs.
  Section 7 (GMM Arellano-Bond) provides a formal bias-corrected estimate.


